==Trivia==
*While Daybreaker Izanagi may look feminine, they are directly based on [[wikipedia:Izanagi|Izanagi]] ("He-who-invites" or "Male-who-invites"), one of the primordial central deities of the Japanese creation myth. Together, Izanagi and his sister-wife [[Izanami of Dusk (Legend Rare Cat)|Izanami]] are said to have created the islands of Japan and many of the Shinto gods who came to inhabit them, such as [[Shining Amaterasu (Uber Rare Cat)|Amaterasu]], who is considered one of Izanagi's "Three Precious Children", and [[Good-Luck Ebisu (Super Rare Cat)|Ebisu]], who is sometimes identified with the twins' misconceived firstborn son Hiruko. The floating spear next to the Cat Unit is [[wikipedia:Ame-no-Nuboko|Ame-no-Nuboko]], a jeweled spear that the twin gods used to stir the ocean, creating the first Japanese island in mythology, [[wikipedia:Onogoro Island|Onogoroshima]], from the brine that fell from the spear's tip and back into the sea.
**Izanagi, Amaterasu and Ebisu all have abilities targeting every trait, and Izanagi's Insane Damage ability is a stronger version of Amaterasu's Massive Damage.
*They and [[Master of Mind Soractes (Special Cat)|Master of Mind Soractes]] were the first units to receive the Conjure ability.

